        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is Tru Grit a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Tru Grit makes two curved manual treadmills that are among the cheapest with sled-push resistance. Reviews are mixed on build quality, the brand publishes few figures, and its website was not working on 5 November 2026. The standard Grit Runner is a reasonable budget buy from a dealer that will handle warranty claims.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the Tru Grit Runner curved manual treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 5 November 2026 US dealers listed it from $1,996 at Push Pedal Pull (on sale from $2,495) to $2,699 at American Fitness, with $2,359 at Select Fitness and $2,495 at iSellFitness and The Fitness Outlet. Total Fitness USA listed it at $3,299. Prices change often.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the Tru Grit Runner weight limit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Every dealer listing we read gives 330 lb for the standard Grit Runner. Tru Grit does not publish a weight rating for the Grit Runner Elite, as TreadmillReviews.com also notes, so ask the dealer for it in writing.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Grit Runner and the Grit Runner Elite?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The standard Runner has six resistance levels split into running, walking and sled-push settings and a basic battery LCD. The Elite has four magnetic resistance levels with a dual-belt transmission and a Bluetooth and ANT+ console. On 5 November 2026 the Elite was $3,495 against $1,996 to $3,299 for the Runner.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does Tru Grit give?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Dealers list a lifetime frame warranty on the Grit Runner, with two years on the resistance belt, tread and monitor. For the Elite, dealers disagree: one lists lifetime frame and belt with 5 years on the tread and 3 on the monitor. Ask your dealer who handles claims.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Tru Grit Runner on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. An Amazon listing titled Tru Grit Fitness Runner Curved Manual, with six resistance levels and an LCD, matched the standard Grit Runner on 4 November 2026. We did not find an Amazon listing for the Elite. Check the seller and warranty before buying.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Tru Grit Runner good for HYROX training?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is one of the cheapest curved treadmills with settings designed for sled pushes, which makes it a budget option for HYROX-style running and push work. The official HYROX race treadmill, the Centr x HYROX Perform Tread, has eight magnetic levels and costs $6,999.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

